# Vulnerabilities the Rust dependency audit (cargo-audit.sh, the `dependency-audit` job) is told to accept. One advisory id per line, and
# EVERY entry needs a reason above it and an expiry, so it comes back for a decision instead of being forgotten:
#
#   # RUSTSEC-2026-0001 in foo 1.2.3: only reachable on Linux through Tauri's GTK layer, fixed in Tauri 2.12 (checked 2026-11-05, see #NNN).
#   RUSTSEC-2026-0001 exp:2027-01-31
#
# Only a VULNERABILITY can fail the audit, so only those need an entry. `unmaintained`, `unsound` and `yanked` advisories are listed in the
# job summary and never fail it. Never accept an advisory you have not read.
